<!--meta {"lead": "A rating summary shows a braider's published-review score and how many reviews it comes from, so Maya can judge Nia at a glance without trusting a number that hides how little evidence it has.", "description": "Score with star and review count, compact score for one review, and the honest unrated state.", "pills": ["Published reviews only", "Status: stable"], "variants": "summary (score + count), score only (one review), unrated", "states": "static; rated, unrated", "sources": ["pages/matching-braiders/default", "pages/braider-profile/default", "pages/braider-profile/empty"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a rating summary wherever a braider's reputation is shown: matching results, the profile head and the reviews section. It reads only from published reviews (L2-008). When a braider has none, it says <b>Not yet rated</b> rather than showing 0 or a placeholder score. It is read-only; collecting a rating uses a horizontal <a href="radio-group.html">radio group</a>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure"><span class="rating"><span aria-hidden="true" class="rating__visual">{{icon:star|icon--sm icon--fill rating__star}}<span class="rating__value">4.9</span> <span class="rating__count">· 86 reviews</span></span><span class="visually-hidden">Rated 4.9 out of 5 from 86 reviews</span></span></figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Star</b><small>Filled 16px star, <code>--rating-star</code>; decorative.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Value</b><small>One decimal, label weight, tabular figures.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Count</b><small>"· 86 reviews", muted body-small.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Spoken text</b><small>Visually hidden: "Rated 4.9 out of 5 from 86 reviews"; the visual part is <code>aria-hidden</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:Summary, score for one review, unrated.}}
<span class="rating"><span aria-hidden="true" class="rating__visual">{{icon:star|icon--sm icon--fill rating__star}}<span class="rating__value">4.9</span> <span class="rating__count">· 86 reviews</span></span><span class="visually-hidden">Rated 4.9 out of 5 from 86 reviews</span></span>
<span class="rating"><span aria-hidden="true" class="rating__visual">{{icon:star|icon--sm icon--fill rating__star}}<span class="rating__value">5</span></span><span class="visually-hidden">Rated 5 out of 5</span></span>
<span class="rating rating--unrated">Not yet rated</span>
  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="One size; it inherits body-small and sits beside card titles and profile names."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <p>Static and never focusable. The two data states are rated and unrated; a braider whose only reviews are pending moderation is unrated.</p>
  {{themes}}<span class="rating"><span aria-hidden="true" class="rating__visual">{{icon:star|icon--sm icon--fill rating__star}}<span class="rating__value">4.8</span> <span class="rating__count">· 64 reviews</span></span><span class="visually-hidden">Rated 4.8 out of 5 from 64 reviews</span></span><span class="rating rating--unrated">Not yet rated</span>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul><li>Wraps between value and count only when its container is narrower than about 9rem; the star always stays with the value.</li><li>Large counts use thousands separators: "· 1,284 reviews".</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p><code>--rating-star</code> aliases <code>--color-warning-icon</code> (amber-500 light, amber-300 dark). Value text uses <code>--color-fg-default</code>, the count <code>--color-fg-muted</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3><p>Plain text; no role. The visual part is hidden from assistive technology and one sentence is read instead, so "star 4.9 dot 86 reviews" is never announced.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3><table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Skips it; not focusable.</td></tr></tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3><p>None.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3><p>The hidden sentence carries the score and count. The star is decorative, so its colour needs no non-text contrast; the value carries the meaning.</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Value|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Count|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3><p>None.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3><p>Not a target.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul><li>One decimal for averages ("4.9"), none for a single review ("5").</li><li>"1 review", "86 reviews"; never "86 ratings".</li><li>Unrated copy is "Not yet rated", never "0.0" or "New".</li></ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="rating rating--unrated">Not yet rated</span></div><figcaption>Jules has no published reviews, so the summary says so.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="rating"><span class="rating__value">0.0</span> <span class="rating__count">· 0 reviews</span></span></div><figcaption>A zero score reads as a terrible braider, not an unknown one.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span class="rating"><span aria-hidden="true" class="rating__visual">{{icon:star|icon--sm icon--fill rating__star}}<span class="rating__value">4.9</span> <span class="rating__count">· 86 reviews</span></span><span class="visually-hidden">Rated 4.9 out of 5 from 86 reviews</span></span></div><figcaption>An SVG star with hidden spoken text.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><span>4.9 ★ · 86 reviews</span></div><figcaption>A text glyph, as in the first mocks: read aloud as "black star".</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    {{tok:Star|--color-warning-icon}}
    {{tok:Value|--color-fg-default}}
    {{tok:Count|--color-fg-muted}}
    {{tok:Gap|--space-1}}
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p>Component token: <code>--rating-star</code>.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;span class="rating"&gt;
  &lt;span aria-hidden="true" class="rating__visual"&gt;&lt;svg class="icon icon--sm icon--fill rating__star"&gt;…&lt;/svg&gt;
    &lt;span class="rating__value"&gt;4.9&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="rating__count"&gt;· 86 reviews&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
  &lt;span class="visually-hidden"&gt;Rated 4.9 out of 5 from 86 reviews&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="rating rating--unrated"&gt;Not yet rated&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/default|summary on each result; Jules unrated}}
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/default|profile head and reviews section}}
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/empty|unrated profile}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed: the first mocks wrote ratings as text with a ★ glyph ("4.9 ★ · 86 reviews") and had no unrated state.</p>
</section>
